PROMPT 8 — ROUTELESS CRISIS CONTROL CENTER
ROLE

Act as a senior emergency transportation systems architect.

Continue the existing ROUTELESS project.

OBJECTIVE

Build a complete Crisis Control Center integrated into the existing transportation application.

CRISIS DASHBOARD

Display:

Total buses.
Operational buses.
Broken-down buses.
Available seats.
Normal student demand.
Emergency demand.
Examination students.
Road closures.
Affected routes.
Students requiring transportation.
Students assigned.
Students waiting.
Students expected to arrive on time.
Students expected to arrive late.

Calculate statistics from actual demonstration records.

EMERGENCY EVENTS

Support:

BUS BREAKDOWN.
ROAD BLOCKAGE.
FLOODING.
DEMAND SURGE.
DRIVER UNAVAILABLE.
OTHER TRANSPORTATION EMERGENCY.

Each event must have an ID, type, affected resource, timestamp, severity, verification status and active status.

CRISIS SCENARIO

Create a repeatable simulation:

ACTIVATE EXAMINATION DAY CRISIS

Simulate simultaneously:

Two buses becoming unavailable.
Demand increasing by 40%.
One major road becoming flooded.
Multiple students having examinations within two hours.
Limited operational bus capacity.

The system must update the actual application data.

CRISIS WORKFLOW
Disable affected buses.
Block flooded road segments.
Recalculate available capacity.
Identify affected students.
Identify examination priorities.
Trigger emergency route calculation.
Prepare allocation inputs.
Display affected students and resources.

Include:

RESET SIMULATION.

Reset all modified data to its original seeded state.

OFFLINE CRISIS SUPPORT

Display saved emergency plans and timestamps.

Prepare integration with the offline tiny-signal mechanism.

Never imply a disconnected device has received a new remote alert.

ACCEPTANCE TESTS
Crisis activates correctly.
Two buses become unavailable.
Flooded road is excluded.
Demand increases by 40%.
Examination records are recognized.
Dashboard statistics update from actual records.
Reset restores original data.
Crisis events are auditable.

Implement actual functionality, not static dashboard numbers.
